slml 0.2
use"layout.slml"

@box{bg#e8edff p10 r8}

doc{$title"Layout"
  t.lead"Layout is part of SLML. Four containers, `column`, `row`, `grid` and `page`, and a handful of attributes describe almost any page."
  section{$id"column-row" $title"Columns and rows"
    "`column` stacks its children from top to bottom, `row` places them side by side. `gap` is the space between them."
    demo{$code"column(gap: 8) {\n  text.box \"One\"\n  row(gap: 8) {\n    text.box \"Two\"\n    text.box \"Three\"\n  }\n}"
      c{g8
        t.box"One"
        r{g8
          t.box"Two"
          t.box"Three"
        }
      }
    }
    "The `page` itself is a column with 32 pixels of padding and a gap of 16."
  }
  section{$id"sizes" $title"Sizes: auto, fill and pixels"
    "`width` and `height` take three kinds of values:"
    c{g0
      ref{$name"auto" $values"default" $about"As big as the content. In a column, auto width fills the column unless align says otherwise."}
      ref{$name"fill" $values"share space" $about"Take the free space. Several fill children share it equally."}
      ref{$name"240" $values"pixels" $about"Exactly this size, padding and border included."}
    }
    demo{$code"row(gap: 8) {\n  text.box(width: 80) \"80 px\"\n  text.box(width: fill) \"fill\"\n  text.box(width: fill) \"fill\"\n  text.box \"auto\"\n}"
      r{g8
        t.box{w80 "80 px"}
        t.box{w:f "fill"}
        t.box{w:f "fill"}
        t.box"auto"
      }
    }
    "`max-width` limits a size and `min-width` sets a lower bound. They are the key to readable pages: `column(width: fill, max-width: 760)` is a column that grows with the window but never gets too wide."
  }
  section{$id"align" $title"Alignment"
    "`align` places children across the container (horizontally in a column, vertically in a row): `start`, `center`, `end` or `stretch` (the default). `justify` distributes them along it: `start`, `center`, `end` or `between`."
    demo{$code"row(justify: between, align: center, fill: #f4f4f8, padding: 10) {\n  text.box \"Left\"\n  text.box(padding: 20) \"Middle\"\n  text.box \"Right\"\n}\ncolumn(align: center) { text.box \"Centered\" }"
      r{j:b a:c bg#f4f4f8 p10
        t.box"Left"
        t.box{p20 "Middle"}
        t.box"Right"
      }
      c{a:c t.box"Centered"}
    }
    "A `spacer` absorbs free space; it is the easiest way to push things apart:"
    code"row { text \"Logo\"  spacer  text \"Menu\" }"
  }
  section{$id"responsive" $title"Responsive layouts"
    "Pages are viewed on phones and wide screens. Two tools adapt a layout to the space available:"
    "*Wrapping rows.* With `wrap: true`, children that don't fit move to the next line. Give `fill` children a `min-width` to say how narrow they may get:"
    demo{$code"row(wrap: true, gap: 8) {\n  text.box(width: fill, min-width: 160) \"Sidebar\"\n  text.box(width: fill, min-width: 260) \"Content\"\n}"
      r{wrap g8
        t.box{w:f nw160 "Sidebar"}
        t.box{w:f nw260 "Content"}
      }
    }
    "*Grids.* `grid(columns: 3)` makes three equal columns. `grid(cell-width: 200)` fits as many columns of at least 200 pixels as the width allows: four on a laptop, one on a phone."
    demo{$code"grid(cell-width: 140, gap: 8) {\n  text.box \"A\"  text.box \"B\"  text.box \"C\"\n  text.box \"D\"  text.box \"E\"\n}"
      grid{cw140 g8
        t.box"A"
        t.box"B"
        t.box"C"
        t.box"D"
        t.box"E"
      }
    }
    note{$title"Try it"
      "Make this browser window narrower: the sidebar of this handbook moves above the text and the grid above drops columns. Both are just a wrapping row and a grid."
    }
  }
  section{$id"recipes" $title"Recipes"
    t{b "Centered page content"}
    code"""
        page(align: center) {
          column(width: fill, max-width: 760, gap: 20) { ... }
        }
        """
    t{b "Header with logo and menu"}
    code"""
        row(align: center, gap: 16, padding: 16) {
          image(src: "/logo.png", alt: "Home", width: 32, to: "/index.slml")
          spacer
          text { link(to: "/about.slml") "About" }
          text { link(to: "/contact.slml") "Contact" }
        }
        """
    t{b "Sidebar layout that stacks on phones"}
    code"""
        row(wrap: true, gap: 24) {
          column(width: 240) { ...menu... }
          column(width: fill, min-width: 320) { ...content... }
        }
        """
  }
  pager{$prev"/text.slml" $prev-label"Text" $next"/styling.slml" $next-label"Boxes and styles"}
}
